<content>
  <section><para>The table gives predictions of the average costs of a gasoline car after the year 2030.</para>
<para>Which graph best represents the relationship between time and the predicted cost?</para>
<table>
  <tgroup cols="2"><caption>
  Gasoline car
  </caption>
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry> Time (years) </entry>
      <entry> Cost (thousand of dollars) </entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry> 0 </entry>
      <entry> 35 </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry> 5 </entry>
      <entry> 40.2 </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry> 10 </entry>
      <entry> 46.3 </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry> 15 </entry>
      <entry> 53.2 </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry> 20 </entry>
      <entry> 61.2 </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</tgroup></table>
</section>
</content>
